# Amazon Prime Ecosystem Value Model

## Prime Flywheel Components (2025 Data)

### Prime Membership Metrics
- Total Subscribers Worldwide: 220M
- Total US Subscribers: 200M
- Annual Membership Revenue (2024): $44.374B
- Q3 2025 Revenue: $12.574B (+11.5% YoY)
- Retention Rate Year 1: 93%
- Retention Rate Year 2: 98%

### Prime Member Spending Analysis
- Prime Member Annual Spend: $1,400
- Non-Prime Member Annual Spend: $600
- Prime Premium: $800 per member
- Total Prime Spending Premium: $176B (220M × $800)

### Prime Service Cost Structure (Estimated)
- Free Shipping Cost: ~$8B annually
- Prime Video Content: ~$7B annually
- Prime Music Licensing: ~$1B annually
- Technology Infrastructure: ~$2B annually
- Total Service Cost: ~$18B annually

### Value Creation Model
- Net Prime Revenue After Costs: $26.374B ($44.374B - $18B)
- Cross-selling Value to AWS: ~$5B (estimated enterprise influence)
- Advertising Targeting Value: ~$3B (Prime data for ads)
- Total Prime Ecosystem Value: ~$34.374B annually

## Negative Cash Conversion Cycle Model

### Working Capital Components (2025)
- Days Sales Outstanding (DSO): 31 days
- Days Inventory Outstanding (DIO): 37 days
- Days Payable Outstanding (DPO): 111 days
- Cash Conversion Cycle: -42 days

### Financing Value Calculation
- Annual Revenue: $716.92B
- Daily Revenue: $1.964B ($716.92B ÷ 365)
- Free Financing from CCC: $82.5B (42 days × $1.964B)
- Estimated Interest Rate Saved: 4.5%
- Annual Interest Savings: $3.7B ($82.5B × 4.5%)

### Supplier Relationship Analysis
- Accounts Payable: $121.9B (2025)
- Average Payment Terms: 111 days
- Estimated Supplier Count: 2M+ globally
- Market Power Leverage: Dominant position enables extended terms